# anbud-core — environment template.
# `.env` is a copy of this file and is GITIGNORED: never commit it and never
# paste its contents into a chat. This template (no secrets) is what is tracked.
#
# Each core owns its own .env. Studio's Compose launcher does not read this
# file because Anbud is not deployed yet: its API currently migrates
# through the runtime DSN, and its dedicated database roles are not provisioned
# in the unified stack. Keep names namespaced (ANBUD_*, DOFFIN_*, TED_*);
# generic names such as PORT collide when core env files are merged.

# ── Doffin Public API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Needed to ingest from Doffin. Without it the service still starts and reports
# the source as "not_configured" (GET /ready, GET /api/v1/sources); it never
# crashes and never silently skips.
#
# Get it from the Doffin API portal
# (https://dof-notices-prod-api.developer.azure-api.net): sign in → your
# subscription to the *Public API* → copy the Primary key.
#   • Public API  = search + download of published notices   ← this one
#   • Notices API = PUBLISHES legally binding notices        ← never put its key here
# Production and test are separate portals; this is the PRODUCTION key. Leave
# the Secondary key unused so the Primary can be rotated without downtime.
DOFFIN_API_KEY=

# The subscription's second key (the portal shows Primary and Secondary). Both
# work and share one budget. Only cmd/doffin-probe reads it, to check it and to
# rotate keys (regenerate one key while the other is in use, then swap). The
# service never loads it. Optional, but not allowed without the primary.
DOFFIN_API_KEY_SECONDARY=

# ── TED (EU notices) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT NEEDED. TED documents that every service reading *published* notices is
# anonymous; a key is only for endpoints that touch notices not yet published
# (publication, validation). Nothing reads this and nothing sends it anywhere.
# Keep it only if you want it stored (TED shows an API key just once).
TED_API_KEY=

# ── Organisation lookups through org-core (Control Plane) ─────────────────────
# Optional. anbud-core never calls Brønnøysund itself: it asks org-core, which owns
# organisations and holds the platform's Enhetsregisteret client
# (GET /api/v1/brreg/{orgnr}, scope org:brreg:read). Set both or neither.
# The token must ALSO be registered in org-core's ORG_CORE_SERVICE_CREDENTIALS
# (Control Plane), as principal "anbud-core", audience "org-core", scope
# "org:brreg:read". 32-512 characters, not starting with test/placeholder/change-me.
# ANBUD_ORG_CORE_URL=http://org-core:8080
# ANBUD_ORG_CORE_TOKEN=

# ── Tender documents (docs/REQUIREMENTS.md section 12) ─────────────────────────
# Opt-in. A company uploads the tender documents it already holds for a notice as a ZIP, and
# the gate reads them. It keeps a company's own documents (the manifest and the sentences that
# name a certificate, not the files and not their text), so it is off until you turn it on, and
# the personal-data questions in docs/PERSONAL-DATA.md (17 to 20) come first for a real tenant.
# ANBUD_TENDER_DOCS=true
# How long an upload is kept before it expires and is purged. A Go duration (no "d" unit):
# 2160h is 90 days; at most 17520h (two years). Checked even when the feature is off.
# ANBUD_TENDER_DOCS_RETENTION=2160h
# The largest archive, 1 to 512 MB. Memory is the cost: size the container for it.
# ANBUD_TENDER_DOCS_MAX_MB=100
# ── Optional tuning (built-in defaults shown; uncomment to override) ───────────
# Doffin documents 30 search and 10 download requests per minute PER KEY. The
# defaults keep ~20% headroom; values above the documented limits are rejected
# at startup.
# DOFFIN_BASE_URL=https://api.doffin.no/public/v2
# Both keys are sent to the host in DOFFIN_BASE_URL, so any host other than
# api.doffin.no is refused unless it is named exactly here. Loopback is for tests.
# DOFFIN_BASE_URL_ALLOW_HOST=
# DOFFIN_SEARCH_RPM=24
# DOFFIN_DOWNLOAD_RPM=8
# DOFFIN_HTTP_TIMEOUT=30s

# ── Anbud API authority and dedicated database ───────────────────────────────
# Required when running Anbud outside the unified Studio Compose. Do not
# reuse the generic DATABASE_URL or INTERNAL_API_KEY without verifying the
# dedicated anbud_core database, role, and service principal first.
# ANBUD_API_KEY=
# ANBUD_DSN=postgres://ingestion_user:<password>@localhost:<postgres-host-port>/anbud_core?sslmode=disable

# ── Database roles (docs/ROLES.md) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional for cmd/doffin-sync. Also required by cmd/api --migrate-only. When set
# it is the schema owner's DSN (role anbud_migrator): the migrations run through it,
# and ANBUD_DSN should be the application role's (anbud_app), which owns nothing and
# so cannot drop or disable the append-only triggers. Unset, one DSN does both, which
# is accepted on a loopback development database and refused on any other host when
# the role is too privileged. A non-loopback DSN must verify the server certificate.
# ANBUD_MIGRATE_DSN=postgres://anbud_migrator:<password>@<host>:<port>/anbud_core?sslmode=verify-full&sslrootcert=<ca.pem>
# The unified Studio stack runs --migrate-only as a one-shot job, then starts
# cmd/api with its runtime role only; the API must not receive the migrator DSN.
# ANBUD_SKIP_MIGRATIONS=true

# ── Verify the Doffin key (read-only: about 15 searches and 1 download) ────────
#   set -a; source .env; set +a; go run ./cmd/doffin-probe -save-dir testdata/captured
